␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ succeeded in 9471ms:
   1: """Customize the KRAS_G12C_NMA clone (HPV_DOSE_REDUCTION_NMA_REVIEW.html) for the
   2: HPV single-dose vs multi-dose topic.
   3: 
   4: Three trial rows representing a small NMA / paired set:
   5:   1. KEN-SHE bivalent vs delayed-control (1-dose efficacy primary)
   6:   2. KEN-SHE nonavalent vs delayed-control (1-dose efficacy primary)
   7:   3. DoRIS bivalent 1-dose vs 3-dose (immunobridging non-inferiority)
   8: 
   9: The first two share the same delayed-control sham arm â€” multi-arm shared-control
  10: caveat is documented in each row's group field, parallel to the OAKS/DERBY PEOM
  11: split pattern used elsewhere in the portfolio.
  12: """
  13: from __future__ import annotations
  14: import sys
  15: from pathlib import Path
  16: 
  17: FILE = Path("HPV_DOSE_REDUCTION_NMA_REVIEW.html")
  18: 
  19: # ---- 1. <title> ----
  20: OLD_TITLE = "<title>RapidMeta Oncology | KRAS G12C Inhibitors in Pretreated KRAS-G12C-Mutated Advanced NSCLC NMA v1.0</title>"
  21: NEW_TITLE = "<title>RapidMeta Vaccines | Single-Dose HPV Vaccination NMA v0.1 (Africa post-2012)</title>"
  22: 
  23: # ---- 2. AUTO_INCLUDE_TRIAL_IDS ----
  24: OLD_AUTO = "const AUTO_INCLUDE_TRIAL_IDS = new Set(['NCT04303780', 'NCT04685135']);"
  25: NEW_AUTO = "const AUTO_INCLUDE_TRIAL_IDS = new Set(['NCT03675256', 'NCT03675256_NONAV', 'NCT02834637']);"
  26: 
  27: # ---- 3. protocol ----
  28: OLD_PROTO = "protocol: { pop: 'Adults with KRAS-G12C-mutated locally advanced unresectable or metastatic NSCLC after >=1 prior line of platinum-based chemotherapy and PD-(L)1 inhibitor', int: 'Sotorasib 960 mg PO QD or Adagrasib 600 mg PO BID (oral KRAS-G12C inhibitors)', comp: 'Docetaxel 75 mg/m2 IV every 3 weeks', out: 'Investigator-assessed progression-free survival (primary in both pivotal trials); overall survival (key secondary)', subgroup: 'Prior PD-(L)1 line, brain metastases, ECOG PS, CNS metastases status', query: '', rctOnly: true, post2015: true },"
  29: NEW_PROTO = "protocol: { pop: 'HIV-negative females aged 9-20 years in sub-Saharan Africa (Kenya: KEN-SHE; Tanzania: DoRIS) with no history of HPV vaccination; KEN-SHE additionally required 1-5 lifetime sexual partners (sexually active cohort)', int: '1, 2, or 3 doses of bivalent (Cervarix HPV 16/18) or nonavalent (Gardasil-9 HPV 6/11/16/18/31/33/45/52/58) HPV vaccine', comp: 'Delayed-vaccination control (meningococcal conjugate vaccine immediately, with delayed HPV vaccine after primary endpoint) for KEN-SHE; 3-dose schedule of the same HPV vaccine for DoRIS (immunobridging non-inferiority)', out: 'Persistent HPV 16/18 infection at 18 months post first-dose (KEN-SHE primary); HPV 16/18 antibody seropositivity at month 24 with non-inferiority margin (DoRIS primary). Backing the WHO SAGE 2022 single-dose HPV-vaccine recommendation', subgroup: 'Vaccine type (bivalent vs nonavalent), dose schedule (1 vs 2 vs 3), age stratum, country (Kenya vs Tanzania)', query: '', rctOnly: true, post2015: true },"
  30: 
  31: # ---- 4. nctAcronyms ----
  32: OLD_ACRO = "nctAcronyms: { 'NCT04303780': 'CodeBreaK 200', 'NCT04685135': 'KRYSTAL-12' },"
  33: NEW_ACRO = "nctAcronyms: { 'NCT03675256': 'KEN-SHE bivalent', 'NCT03675256_NONAV': 'KEN-SHE nonavalent', 'NCT02834637': 'DoRIS 1d-vs-3d bivalent' },"
  34: 
  35: 
  36: # ---- 5. realData â€” surgical replace ----
  37: NEW_REAL_DATA_BODY = """
  38: 
  39:                 // ============================================================
  40:                 // KEN-SHE bivalent â€” 18-month primary endpoint, persistent
  41:                 // HPV 16/18 infection, single-dose bivalent (Cervarix) vs
  42:                 // delayed-meningococcal control. Barnabas RV et al.
  43:                 // NEJM Evid 2022;1:1-10. PMID 35143335.
  44:                 // Kenya: 3 KEMRI sites (Kisumu, Thika, Nairobi).
  45:                 // SHARED-CONTROL CAVEAT: same delayed-control as the
  46:                 // KEN-SHE nonavalent contrast row (NCT03675256_NONAV).
  47:                 // ============================================================
  48: 
  49:                 'NCT03675256': {
  50: 
  51: 
  52:                     name: 'KEN-SHE bivalent', pmid: '35143335', phase: 'IV', year: 2022, tE: 0, tN: 758, cE: 38, cN: 758, group: 'KEN-SHE bivalent (HPV 16/18) single-dose vs delayed-meningococcal control. tE=0 persistent HPV 16/18 infections at 18 mo (immediate-bivalent arm, n=758 mITT). cE=38 (delayed-control arm, n=758). Vaccine efficacy 97.5% (95% CI 81.7-99.7) per modified-ITT analysis. SHARED-CONTROL CAVEAT: same delayed-control as KEN-SHE nonavalent contrast (NCT03675256_NONAV) â€” pool one or apply split-control per Cochrane 23.3.4. Barnabas RV et al. NEJM Evid 2022 (DOI 10.1056/EVIDoa2100046).',
  53: 
  54: 
  55:                     estimandType: 'RR', publishedHR: 0.025, hrLCI: 0.003, hrUCI: 0.183, pubHR: 0.025, pubHR_LCI: 0.003, pubHR_UCI: 0.183,
  56: 
  57: 
  58:                     allOutcomes: [
